  "steps": [
    {
      "index": 1,
      "label": "Parse individual records",
      "intent": "Implement `parse_record(line)` to convert a text line into a dictionary\n- Each line is `|`-separated with six fields: `TYPE|RECORD_ID|ORDER_ID|AMOUNT|CURRENCY|TIMESTAMP`\n- `TYPE` must be `ORDER` or `PAYMENT`, stored as uppercase and case-insensitive\n- An `ORDER_ID` must start with the prefix `ORD-`\n- IDs must be non-empty after trimming\n- Ensure `AMOUNT` has digits, at most one decimal point, possible leading minus sign, and accept up to three fractional digits\n- Amounts with more than three fractional digits should round to cents using round-half-up\n- Return `None` for records with invalid amounts, identifiers, or currency other than `USD`\n- Output a dictionary with fields `type`, `record_id`, `order_id`, `amount`, `currency`, and `timestamp`, or `None`",
      "checkHint": "`parse_record('order|rec1|ORD-001|100.256|USD|2023-10-05 12:34')` returns a valid dictionary",
      "timeShare": 15
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "label": "Load and process records",
      "intent": "Build `load_records(text)` to handle a block of text input\n- Split the text into lines and parse each using `parse_record(line)`\n- Silently skip invalid records and process only valid ones, maintaining input order\n- Keep the first valid occurrence of duplicate record IDs, ignoring later duplicates\n- Manage only records with currency `USD` and valid amounts, as processed by `parse_record`\n- Function does not mutate input objects or store global state",
      "checkHint": "`load_records('order|rec1|ORD-002|123.45|USD|2023-10-05\\npayment|rec2|ORD-003|-50.00|USD|2023-10-06')` processes as two distinct entries",
      "timeShare": 15
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "label": "Calculate payment refunds",
      "intent": "Develop `compute_refunds(records)` to sum valid refund amounts\n- Refunds are identified by negative payment amounts\n- Sum positive values of qualifying negative payment amounts where `order_id` belongs to an existing order\n- Ignore refunds without corresponding orders\n- Return only valid refunds that adhere to the existing-order rule\n- All calculations in integer cents",
      "checkHint": "`compute_refunds([{'type':'PAYMENT','order_id':'ORD-001','amount':-200}])` returns 200 if `ORD-001` is valid",
      "timeShare": 15
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "label": "Match payments to orders",
      "intent": "Create `match_payments(records)` to match payments to orders\n- For each order, a non-refund payment qualifies from the order timestamp to strictly **less than 72 hours** later\n- Choose the earliest qualifying payment, breaking ties by input order\n- Refunds do not match\n- Result includes `order_id`, status (`matched` or `unmatched`), and `amount`\n- An unmatched order has an amount of `0`\n- Function does not mutate input objects",
      "checkHint": "`match_payments([{'type':'ORDER','order_id':'ORD-001','timestamp':'2023-10-01 12:00'},{'type':'PAYMENT','order_id':'ORD-001','amount':100,'timestamp':'2023-10-03 11:59'}])` marks as matched",
      "timeShare": 20
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "label": "Build summary report",
      "intent": "Implement `build_summary(matches, refund_total)` to generate a summary\n- Return a dictionary with keys: `total_orders`, `matched_count`, `refund_total`, `net_total`, `unmatched_ids`\n- `total_orders` is the number of processed orders\n- `matched_count` is the count of records with status `matched`\n- `net_total` is the sum of matched payment amounts minus `refund_total`, with a **minimum of zero**\n- `unmatched_ids` is a deduplicated ascending lexicographic list\n- Include a key named exactly `refund_total` as part of the summary",
      "checkHint": "`build_summary([{'status':'matched','order_id':'ORD-001','amount':100}], 10)` results in positive net total and correct counts",
      "timeShare": 20
    }
  ]
}

